{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cggxz4WKzhSGwDBGpeBp5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Estimated values (not a full fit): Dq ≈ 750 cm⁻¹, B ≈ 640 cm⁻¹, C ≈ 3390 cm⁻¹.** I did not complete a rigorous fit, so these should be treated as approximate.\n\n**What is exact.** For high-spin d⁵, the ⁴A₁(G) and ⁴E(G) levels do not depend on Dq. Their energy above the ⁶A₁ ground state is exactly 10B + 5C. The 23 370 cm⁻¹ band therefore gives:\n\n10B + 5C = 23 370 cm⁻¹\n\n**What is not exact.** B and C cannot be separated from this one relation. Dq and B have to come from the ⁴T₁(G) and ⁴T₂(G) bands (19 180 and 22 130 cm⁻¹). Their energies depend on Dq and B through the 2×2 mixing of ⁴T₁(G) with ⁴T₁(P) and of ⁴T₂(G) with ⁴T₂(D).\n\nI could not reproduce the Tanabe–Sugano matrix elements reliably, so I did not solve that coupled problem numerically. Instead I chose values typical of Mn²⁺ in a chloride lattice (10Dq ≈ 7500 cm⁻¹, B ≈ 640 cm⁻¹). I checked them only against the exact relation above: with B ≈ 640 cm⁻¹, C = (23 370 − 6400)/5 ≈ 3390 cm⁻¹.\n\n**Caveat.** B and C are therefore only as good as the assumed B, and Dq is a literature-typical estimate rather than a result fitted to the 19 180 and 22 130 cm⁻¹ bands. A proper fit needs numerical diagonalisation of the d⁵ Tanabe–Sugano matrices.\n\n{\"Dq\": 750, \"B\": 640, \"C\": 3390, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"C follows from the exact relation 10B+5C = 23370 cm^-1 for the 4A1,4E band, but Dq and B are literature-typical estimates because I did not diagonalise the 4T1 and 4T2 matrices.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":816,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":816,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformat